<%# locals: entries: -- Array<{ label:, href: }>, built by
    components/show.html.erb (see its own comment on exactly what goes into
    this list and why, and on section ids being derived from title text,
    not position). Treats each demo card and each documentation section as
    a chapter of the current component page, the same way a book's table of
    contents would.

    Only ever rendered via content_for(:contents) on a component page that
    has at least one entry -- application.html.erb checks
    content_for?(:contents) to decide whether to give this its own grid
    column at all, so `entries` is never empty here.

    Sticky beneath the fixed header, using the same --docs-header-height
    custom property the header itself sets (application.html.erb) and
    .docs-sidebar already reads (docs.css) -- so this column and the left
    sidebar stop scrolling at the same line. Hidden below the lg breakpoint
    by the column wrapping this partial in the layout, not by anything in
    here: a narrow viewport has no room for a third nav column, and every
    one of these sections is already in reading order just above it. %>
<nav class="docs-contents" aria-label="Contents">
  <h4 class="text-secondary text-uppercase fs-6 mb-2">Contents</h4>
  <div class="list-group list-group-transparent">
    <% entries.each do |entry| %>
      <%= link_to entry[:label], entry[:href], class: "list-group-item list-group-item-action" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</nav>
